.DS_Store
*.pyc
__pycache__/
STATE.md
# The timestamped backups the autosave writes beside it. STATE.md was already
# ignored; these were not, so `git add -A` swept 477 KB of working state into
# the release manifest in a33dfc0, including two files whose own first line
# reads "gitignored, not shipped". Found by a hostile refuter, not by the seal.
STATE.md.bak-*

# Word owner-lock artifacts (embed the editor username)
~$*

# Internal review and planning notes, never shipped. Both spellings: a directory
# one character different, docs/superpowers/, was tracked and shipping exactly
# the category this rule says is never shipped.
.superpowers/
docs/superpowers/

# Compiled documents. The whitepaper is generated FROM the markdown that ships,
# and the tracked copy went stale against it and carried a paragraph of internal
# development history that the markdown had already been scrubbed of.
*.docx

# The install receipt records this machine's absolute install path, which is a
# local fact and a personal one; the receipt is a local record, never shipped.
.brothersbe/install-receipt.json

# The book's worked estate regenerates these two files on every run; they are
# outputs, not fixtures, so the source CSV and the aggregated JSON stay out.
docs/book/estate/orders.csv
docs/book/estate/daily_totals.json

# The built book is a build product of build_book.py, regenerated from the
# chapter markdown and the vendored mermaid.js on every run, never a fixture.
docs/book/BrotherSBE-for-Dummies.html

# The excerpt replay harness writes one shell script per chapter beside the
# chapter while it re-executes that chapter's terminal blocks, and removes it
# when the run finishes. A run that is interrupted leaves one behind, where it
# shows up as untracked in every concurrent session's sweep and as an
# unexplained EXTRA to the install verifier. It is scratch, never a fixture.
docs/book/.replay-*.sh
LANE-CHECKPOINT.patch
LANE-CHECKPOINT.progress
